        "original_id": "3a08e5f9-1d29-503f-b110-cd7e332fbf95",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: TechCrunch Disrupt New York 2016\n- Companies: The Honest Company, AOL, Uber\n- People: Jessica Alba, B.J. Novak, Tim Armstrong, David Plouffe\n- Topics: ethical consumerism\n\nFacts:\n- In 2014, The Honest Company had $170 million in sales.\n- As of August 2015, The Honest Company was valued at $1.7 billion.\n- The Honest Company is an American consumer goods company founded by Jessica Alba that emphasizes household products for ethical consumerism.\n- At TechCrunch Disrupt New York 2016, the conference included hackathons, meet-and-greets with investors, and guest lectures.\n- At TechCrunch Disrupt New York 2016, guest lecturers included Jessica Alba of The Honest Company, B.J. Novak of The Office, Tim Armstrong of AOL, and David Plouffe.\n- At the time described, David Plouffe was a former Obama White House advisor serving on Uber’s board.",
